Source: dynblk
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms, python3, zlib1g-dev,
 liblz4-1 <!nocheck>, libzstd1 <!nocheck>, qemu-utils <!nocheck>
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/minios-linux/dynblk
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: dynblk
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, kmod, mount
Recommends: dynblk-dkms (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests: liblz4-1, libzstd1, zlib1g
Description: self-contained block storage control and offline checker
 Controls the dynblk kernel block device and validates detached format-1
 storage with one native executable. No Python runtime, FUSE implementation,
 filesystem utilities or legacy command aliases are included.
 Provides a mount helper with kernel-managed automatic device cleanup.

Package: dynblk-dkms
Section: kernel
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 3.2.2)
Recommends: dynblk (= ${binary:Version})
Description: self-contained block storage module source for DKMS
 Builds dynblk for Linux 6.12 using DKMS. Matching headers for each target
 kernel are required; other kernel series are not supported.
 Package configuration and kernel updates build and install the module but
 do not request loading it. No storage is created by this package.
